  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 AM EDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nNot much change with this forecast package. Isolated, diurnal, \nshowers and storm chances continue each day across the east TN \nmountains and perhaps the Cumberland Plateau. The main story is the \nbuilding heat due to a strong ridge of high pressure. \n\nThe upcoming week looks to be a rather unpleasant return to hot and \nmuggy conditions as an upper level ridge locks in over the southern \nUnited States. This will lead to temperatures climbing into the 90's \nfor most locations every afternoon this week. And unfortunately \nalong with this the dew points will rise back into the upper 60's to \nlower 70's making for high heat index values near or just above the \ntriple digit mark. It's possible that some of our southern areas may \napproach Heat Advisory criteria at some point. As we get closer to \nthe end of the week, and into Labor Day Weekend, the high may \nretrograde west again as an upper trough swings down into New \nEngland. This may put us back in a northwest flow pattern, which \nwould increase our chances of rain and bring slightly cooler high \ntemps.",
